<title>MALAYSIA: China fats/oil import seen up 25 pct in 1996/97.</title>
<headline>China fats/oil import seen up 25 pct in 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's import of oils and fats is seen rising 25 percent to 3.8 million tonnes in 1996/97 due to lower domestic oilseeds production, a U.N. official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Low level of stocks is also expected to lead to higher purchases, M. Maftei, a commodities expert with the United Nations, said.  </p>
<p>Speaking at the Vegoils, Oilseeds and Meals '97, Maftei said Chinese farmers were expected to favour soybeans over other grains in the current season.</p>
<p>The country's deficit in soybeans and soybean-based products was expected to rise rapidly and import requirements are seen two to three times higher than in 1995/96, Maftei said.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-2307509)</p>
</text>
